Project: Threes helper – mirrored-device state tracker
======================================================

Purpose
- Observe and drive Threes through macOS `iPhone Mirroring`.
- Detect the live board and preview tile.
- Track the small-tile bag (4 red / 4 blue / 4 gray per 12 non-bonus tiles).
- Track bonus-tile eligibility from the visible board state.
- Record enough artifacts to debug any invalid internal state.

Current structure
- `preview_detector.py`
  - Preview detector and board ROI helpers.
  - Uses a fixed relative board crop; the older saturation-based board crop is gone.
- `window_stream.py`
  - Core board/preview classification logic.
  - Owns the tile-cycle model, bonus-tile rules, board rendering, and dataset recorder.
- `mirroring_control.py`
  - Native macOS driver for the `iPhone Mirroring` window.
  - Scene-aware across `title`, `game`, `game_over`, `postgame`, `menu`, `end_confirm`, `phone_in_use`, and `screen_off`.
  - Handles `game_over -> swipe to summary -> Retry -> new game`.
- `state_hunt.py`
  - Shared transition validator and artifact recorder used by both autonomous and observe-only workflows.
- `hunt_invalid_states.py`
  - Repeated self-play harness. Stops on the first invalid tracked state and saves rewindable artifacts.
- `observe_human_game.py`
  - Observe-only harness for user-driven play. Waits for a fresh board by default, validates settled moves, and saves artifacts on failure.
- `scene_refs/`
  - Cropped reference images for the mirrored end-of-game scenes that are hard to classify from low-res fingerprints alone.

Game-model assumptions in code
- Small-tile bag
  - Exactly 4 red, 4 blue, and 4 gray previews per 12 non-bonus inserts.
  - The bag resets after every 12 non-bonus inserts.
- Move geometry
  - Every move is one of `up/down/left/right`.
  - Tiles move by one square at most.
  - Legal merges are `1+2 -> 3` and identical `3+` tiles.
  - A tile can merge at most once per move.
  - The inserted tile lands in one of the eligible freed edge slots for the swipe direction, and those eligible slots are treated as equally likely.
- Bonus tiles
  - Bonus tiles are only eligible once a 48 tile is visible on the board.
  - Candidate bonus values are derived from the current board max.
  - Candidate values are grouped into equal-likelihood contiguous 3-value bundles.
  - Once a bundle is chosen, each of its 3 tiles is equally likely.
  - Bonus probability is modeled independently from the small bag.
- Tracking bootstrap
  - Fresh-game tracking is only seeded from a valid initial board.
  - If the current visible board is not a valid fresh start, tracking is disabled instead of inventing state.
  - Mid-game attach is allowed only for plausible active boards: no unknown cells, not all empty, and still containing the mandatory 48+ anchor tile.

Tracking and recovery behavior
- `tracker_runtime.py` validates every observed move against the 4 legal swipe directions plus eligible spawn slots.
- Gray-number repairs are legality-aware: they only resolve to a unique legal move candidate with sufficient raw classifier support.
- `live_debug_server.py` keeps the normal path single-frame for responsiveness.
- The live dashboard now separates `visible board` from `committed tracker state`:
  - the visible board may come from a fast candidate frame immediately
  - the tracker still advances only after a legality-valid move event
- If a move would otherwise go invalid, the live tracker now retries across future frames without blocking the main capture loop.
- The dashboard `Start New Game` action uses:
  - in-Threes path: exit current game -> title -> new game
  - out-of-Threes path: home -> search `Threes` -> launch -> new game

Latency notes
- For live debugging, prefer `--capture-backend screen` when the iPhone Mirroring window is visible and unobscured.
- `screen` captures the actual visible pixels on the desktop and is materially fresher than window-buffer capture for iPhone Mirroring.
- `quartz` and `screencapture` remain available fallbacks when the mirrored window is hidden or occluded.
- The live server can auto-fallback when the requested capture backend becomes slow or starts failing.
- `benchmark_live_latency.py` has:
  - `--mode direct` for raw capture + legality timing
  - `--mode server` for end-to-end dashboard/API timing
- The benchmark waits for a settled board before each sample; otherwise the numbers are polluted by the previous move still animating.

Operational notes
- Generated debugging artifacts live under:
  - `datasets/state_hunt/`
  - `datasets/human_watch/`
- Temporary crops and dumped tiles are ignored by `.gitignore`.
- The clean validation baseline for the current driver is:
  - `python3 hunt_invalid_states.py --games 5 --start-from-title --move-order cycle`
  - This completed without a tracked invalid state after the latest scene/bootstrap fixes.

